    "file": "ext/sqlite3/database.c",
    "line": 738,
    "claim": "Ruby callbacks invoked directly from SQLite C code (authorizer, collation compare, busy handler, trace) have no rb_protect, so a Ruby exception longjmps through SQLite frames and skips SQLite's cleanup. The sibling UDF and aggregate paths do wrap their Ruby calls in rb_protect.",
    "source": "Application-registered Ruby callables (set_authorizer database.c:757-775, collation database.c:851-872, busy_handler database.c:386-410, trace database.c:339-357). The attacker does not control the callback. Its trigger is a raising callback, reached via attacker-influenced SQL text (authorizer) or stored data (collation).",
    "sink": "rb_funcall at database.c:738 (rb_sqlite3_auth), database.c:839 (rb_comparator_func, plus NUM2INT at :841), database.c:365 (rb_sqlite3_busy_handler), database.c:328 (tracefunc)",
